name sat-09-gate-strike-1
timeout 460
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; the criteria: doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2.
#
# THE MARGIN, IN THE HEAD, AS A NUMBER, and this file has TWO kinds so both are quoted:
#   the RELEASE GATE   the primary quantity. `ccip-tight` takes the package from 4 releases to **0** —
#                      a structural refusal, lever length effectively infinite, and the four `kill`
#                      bits it costs are therefore not a threshold crossing at all. What still has to
#                      keep a margin is the SEED's own delivery: the aim points sit at the FIXED POINT
#                      of their own release lattice, [MESS] baseline impact 0.0 m from the target and
#                      the two bias rails at +-23.7 m against the Mk 82's 45 m fail radius — **21.3 m**
#                      of margin on both sides, so `bias-early`/`bias-late` are INERT. That is
#                      doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4a satisfied rather than evaded: the file measures the
#                      DECISION (`accepted=`, `releases`) and never a 23 m lever against a 45 m radius.
#   the CYLINDERS      14 `avoid zone` rungs carrying the escort's picture. Narrowest half-gap 1.45 s
#                      against a MEASURED chaos amplitude of 0.10 s over the +-3 m spawn grid —
#                      **15x**; widest 7.80 s (78x).
#
# WHY THE ESCORT'S AMPLITUDE IS 0.10 s: the air half is DRY on both sides (`brief_master_arm sim`), so
# no missile ever leaves a rail and no discrete event amplifies a 3 m perturbation. [MESS] 0
# `damage KILL` among aircraft, 0 `monitor KO`, every `survive` met on every lever. The strike half is
# WET and is the only place a weapon comes off — which is exactly the half this file is about.
#
# WHY A RUNG LADDER: the outcome class is (V, M) and M is a SUM, so a lever that changes WHICH bit is
# met without changing HOW MANY is invisible to it. Each rung sits at the MIDPOINT of a measured gap in
# one continuous dwell, which turns that dwell into a COUNT the class can see. [MESS] `es3`'s dwell in
# `zg2` takes 10 distinct values from 0.0 to 30.2 s over the 25 levers; its seven rungs resolve eight
# of them.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (the arena's own table, 25 levers, `--elev const`):
#   live    G1 shape 6 of 6:  shape-abreast (23,19)  shape-flat (22,19)  shape-stacked (22,19)
#                             shape-tight (22,19)  shape-trail (23,24)  shape-wide (22,20).
#                             THE WHOLE FAMILY, including `shape-trail`, which is inert on every other
#                             rig in this tree — a trail step is 1 852 m of along-track station and
#                             only a cylinder read at a DECLARED instant can see it.
#   live    G5 emcon 3 of 3:  emcon-mid (24,26)  emcon-tight (24,26)  emcon-wide (23,22)
#   live    G3 net   1 of 2:  net-off (23,22);  `sort-left`/`sort-near` are dead beside a live net
#   live    G7 ccip  1 of 2:  ccip-tight (18,18), 4 releases -> 0;  ccip-open INERT (2 000 m accepts
#                             what the seed's own tolerance already did)
#   part    G6 bias  1 of 3:  `bias-rail` only (18,19) — 2.3 km of track, i.e. no delivery at all, and
#                             therefore NOT a mover anybody may read as a direction
#   INERT   G2 cover 0 of 3, G4 energy 0 of 3: inert by airframe and by task
#   BASELINE (22, 23), duration 460.0 s.  12 movers of 24, 11 excluding `bias-rail`; 9 distinct
#   classes; modal share 52.0 % (13 of 25).  S1 ok, S2 ok.
#   S7: [MESS] **0 of 8** spawn perturbations on the 0.8 m grid flip the baseline class.
#
# AND THE CLOCK: the duration takes two values, 460.0 s (the timeout) and 260.1 s (`emcon-mid`,
# `emcon-tight`, where every unit had concluded because every window had closed). 260.1 s IS the
# instant every objective here was frozen at, so the short runs cannot have truncated anything graded.
#
# THE ARENA: a four-ship CCIP strike at 900 m on four soft aim points, escorted by a dry four-ship
# against a dry four-ship MiG-29 CAP under a GCI brief. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking
# (C4). Every coordinate is [SET] except the four aim points, which are the converged fixed point
# above. Day, 11:00 local.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH THE ESCORT UNABLE TO SHOOT AND THE STRIKE UNABLE TO BE SHOT AT, WHAT
# DOES THE PACKAGE'S DOCTRINE DO TO THE STRIKERS' RELEASE DECISION?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log         `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE unit=st* accepted=` — THE PRIMARY CHANNEL, the decision
#                      itself; `mission WINDOW_CLOSED` at t = 260.1; `zone ENTER`/`EXIT`;
#                      `sms RELEASE_REJECTED` on the escorts (the dry proof)
#   telemetry_es*.csv  `zone_zg1_s`, `zone_zg2_s`, `zone_zg3_s` — the dwells the ladders read
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED exit and is NOT the measurement; a duration
# below 460 s is not one either, because it can only be the instant the last window closed. THE
# MEASUREMENT IS (V, M) SUMMED OVER THE EIGHT F-16 — 14 `avoid zone` rungs, 4 `kill unit` and 8
# `survive`, 26 objectives — AND ITS SPREAD ACROSS THE LEVER SET. A single run measures NOTHING. A
# reader who quotes the number of targets destroyed has answered a question this file does not ask:
# what is being measured is whether the doctrine let the pickle happen at all.

zone zg1 33.24000 44.44000 9000 0 12000

zone zg2 33.24000 44.60000 6000 0 12000

zone zg3 33.32000 44.60000 4000 0 12000

unit es1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight es 1
  spawn 33.36000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.36000 45.00000 6000 480
  objective survive until 260

